      "extract": "A related question is to bound the number of solutions to (6.1) in the group of units O× K. Evertse [14] proved that the number of solutions to x1 + x2 = 1 with x1, x2 ∈O× K is at most 3 · 73d, where d is the degree of K. (Such xi are often called ‘exceptional units’.) Niklasch [34] considered this question further and in particular, generalising a conjecture of Stewart (see [15, p.120]), conjectured [34, Conjecture",
