      "extract": "We now explain the $p$-adic variant. If the field $K$ in Lemma [\\[lem-main\\]](#lem-main){reference-type=\"ref\" reference=\"lem-main\"} has a prime lying over $p$ that is split, for example, if $p$ splits completely in $K$, then $K$ embeds into $\\mathbb Q_p$ and thus the set $A \\subseteq \\mathcal O_K$ constructed in Lemma [\\[lem-main\\]](#lem-main){reference-type=\"ref\" reference=\"lem-main\"} embeds into $\\mathbb Z_p$.",
